{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0173a8cd-0c8c-4488-9947-47ad469980ce","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7b6c51190c2993d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-fyrp5ktx/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers a run comparison surface in the Dashboard: users select two or more\ntraining or pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side,\nwith a diff presentation that highlights which parameters and metrics changed\nbetween two selected runs. This replaces the exported-spreadsheet workflow\ndescribed in the strategy's problem statement with an in-platform comparison.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of two or more runs from the existing runs list in the\n  Dashboard.\n- A comparison view rendering the parameters and metrics of every selected\n  run side by side.\n- Diff presentation for two selected runs: parameters and metrics that\n  changed between the two runs are highlighted. The strategy states this as\n  the same comparison surface — the diff is a presentation mode of the\n  side-by-side view over the same run data — so it is delivered together\n  with the multi-run comparison rather than as a separate effort.\n- The comparison renders data for both training runs and pipeline runs\n  through the run data interfaces the Dashboard already consumes for its\n  per-run pages. Data Science Pipelines requires no code changes for this\n  (passive component); its correct interaction is validated as an\n  acceptance criterion of this epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the runs list in the Dashboard, a user can select two or more runs\n  and open a comparison of them.\n- The comparison view displays the parameters and metrics of all selected\n  runs side by side.\n- Given exactly two selected runs, the comparison highlights which\n  parameters and metrics differ between the two runs.\n- The comparison renders correctly for pipeline runs sourced from Data\n  Science Pipelines and for training runs — passive-component validation\n  that run parameters and metrics feed the comparison unchanged through the\n  existing run data interfaces, with no Data Science Pipelines code\n  changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters\n  and metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1): run diff view highlighting which parameters and metrics\n  changed between two selected runs — bundled with HLR-1 because it is a\n  presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data;\n  a separate epic would build the same surface twice.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34553,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b974168bd82785d3","agent_id":"aaee05bc5df011cdd","session_id":"2f8acaed-d2b4-4961-b36e-484262868126","uuid":"f1d60600-085e-4158-8c0d-60edee6a41bf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:26.361Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
