{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e6ffac0c214031e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\tFull decomposition (not triaged): the strategy spans multiple components and\n13\tteams (Dashboard, Model Registry, Data Science Pipelines), so neither Step 0\n14\tcheck applies. Open Questions section states \"None\"; no conditional ADRs,\n15\tpending reviews, or risks are recorded, so no Investigation epics were created.\n16\tAll three affected components exist in `.context/architecture-context/`\n17\t(`dashboard.md`, `model-registry.md`, `data-science-pipelines.md` — all GA and\n18\tKonflux onboarded), so no onboarding chain is needed.\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Run lineage on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open a run comparison from the Model Registry | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Documentation for the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n28\t\n29\t## Dependency DAG\n30\t\n31\t```mermaid\n32\tgraph TD\n33\t    E001 --> E003\n34\t    E002 --> E003\n35\t    E001 --> E004\n36\t    E002 --> E004\n37\t    E003 --> E004\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t## DAG Justification\n41\t\n42\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n43\t|------|------|-----------|\n44\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework/surface → consumer) | The registry entry point opens and builds against the run comparison surface; it is a consumer of that surface, not an independent build of it. |\n45\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact-producing → consuming Implementation) | The registry entry point consumes the run reference recorded on registered model versions; without the lineage artifact there is nothing to link from. |\n46\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation describes the comparison capability that was built. |\n47\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 | Documentation describes the model-version run lineage. |\n48\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 | Documentation describes the registry-side entry point of the comparison workflow. |\n49\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Dashboard (odh-dashboard) and Model Registry (model-registry) are separate repos with no shared build artifacts; both start in parallel. |\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n52\t\n53\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n54\t|-----|----------|---------|\n55\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 |\n56\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002, E003 |\n57\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (bundled) — the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1 (the strategy itself notes wording overlap kept from two consolidated customer councils); a separate epic would build the same surface twice plus an artificial serialization edge |\n58\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 |\n59\t\n60\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n61\t\n62\t## Health Warnings\n63\t\n64\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n65\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no formal Acceptance Criteria\n66\t  (Given/When/Then), and no Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were derived\n67\t  from the architecture-context owning teams (RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry,\n68\t  RHOAI Pipelines); epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n69\t- **Passive component — Data Science Pipelines**: listed as affected but\n70\t  requires no code changes — run parameters and metrics already surface on\n71\t  per-run pages in the Dashboard (per the problem statement and\n72\t  `data-science-pipelines.md`, pipeline runs surface in the Dashboard via the\n73\t  KFP v2 API). Validation became an acceptance criterion on E001: the\n74\t  comparison must render pipeline-run data correctly. No separate\n75\t  validation epic was generated because the strategy assigns no\n76\t  Data Science Pipelines-team validation work — the validation is exercised\n77\t  as part of the comparison feature's own acceptance testing by the\n78\t  Dashboard team.\n79\t- **HLR-1 / HLR-3 redundancy**: consolidated into the single comparison epic\n80\t  (E001) at the higher priority (P0) per the redundant-HLR rule; see the\n81\t  traceability row above for the inline rationale.\n82\t- **Docs epic priority**: HLR-4 is P2, but per the docs-authoring priority\n83\t  exception the epic priority derives from the strategy frontmatter\n84\t  (`priority: Major` → P1).\n85\t- **Docs epic team note**: the documentation epic is assigned to the\n86\t  RHOAI Dashboard team (owner of the primary comparison surface); the\n87\t  registry-lineage sections must be reviewed with the Model Registry team,\n88\t  which is enforced by the epic's technical-review acceptance criterion.\n89\t- **HLR-2 split across components**: HLR-2 spans two components and is\n90\t  covered by two epics — the Model Registry lineage data (E002) and the\n91\t  Dashboard registry-side entry point (E003). The Dashboard half was kept\n92\t  out of the P0 comparison epic so the P0 surface is not gated on registry\n93\t  work, and out of E002 because epic components must be single canonical\n94\t  names (Dashboard vs Model Registry).\n95\t\n96\t## Tiered Delivery\n97\t\n98\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n99\tintra-platform.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2d5b1089e0b73b1","agent_id":"a0f0da0279c6cdfce","session_