ndencies; all referenced epics exist. Cross-checked every\n41\tdiagram edge against frontmatter `dependencies` in both directions:\n42\tE001→E003, E002→E003, E001→E004, E002→E004, E003→E004 match E003's\n43\t[E001, E002] and E004's [E001, E002, E003] exactly; E001 and E002 have none.\n44\tArrows run dependency→dependent per convention. Each edge is justified under\n45\tthe construction rules: E001→E003 is Rule 12 (E003 builds against the\n46\tcomparison surface E001 delivers); E002→E003 is Rule 13 (E003's Dashboard\n47\tcode builds against the run-reference retrieval API E002 exposes — a\n48\tbuild-against API artifact, not a configuration reference, so an edge rather\n49\tthan an AC gate is the rule-compliant shape); the three edges into E004 are\n50\tRule 11 docs-last. E001 ∥ E002 parallelism is correctly preserved (Rule 14,\n51\tseparate repos odh-dashboard vs model-registry, no shared artifacts). No\n52\timplementation-type parallelism rules (7/8/10) apply — no konflux-onboarding,\n53\tlicense-validation, or repo-onboarding epics exist (all three components are\n54\talready Konflux-onboarded per `.context`). Critical path 3\n55\t(E001→E003→E004) is the rule-mandated minimum for this shape: 2 for the\n56\timplementation chain plus the mandatory Rule 11 docs tail. Content\n57\tcross-check found no uncaptured data/artifact dependencies.\n58\t\n59\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n60\tEach epic carries a single canonical component and team (Dashboard/RHOAI\n61\tDashboard for E001, E003; Model Registry/Model Registry for E002;\n62\tDocumentation/RHOAI Dashboard for E004). The HLR-2 split along the component\n63\tseam (E002 data vs E003 UI) is correct under Rule 1, and keeping E003 out of\n64\tthe P0 epic so the P0 surface is not coupled to registry work is a sound,\n65\trecorded trade-off. E001 vs E003 is not scope duplication: E003 is an entry\n66\tpoint that consumes E001's surface and E002's run-reference artifact rather\n67\tthan rebuilding either, and it is gated on a cross-component deliverable —\n68\tneither epic independently builds the other's work. The HLR-1/HLR-3\n69\tpresentation-mode bundling in E001 follows the one-epic-per-surface rule.\n70\tNo epic is oversized for the ~2-week guideline; code implementation and\n71\tcontent authoring are properly separated (E004 is the only docs epic). No\n72\theterogeneous bundling and no work-type mixing found.\n73\t\n74\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n75\tAll four epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (UI\n76\tsurface, API-backed lineage data, entry-point action, published docs). No\n77\tInvestigation epics exist, which is correct: the strategy records no open\n78\tquestions, risks, or pending decisions whose outcomes would change downstream\n79\tscope or existence. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set, and\n80\tnone are required. `implementation_type` is null for the three general\n81\timplementation epics (valid — it is an optional routing label) and\n82\t`docs-authoring` on E004 is correct.\n83\t\n84\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n85\tAll epics are Implementation type and correctly carry `ai_signals` (the\n86\t9-signal set); no epic mixes in `investigation_signals`. Frontmatter values\n87\tmatch the rationale tables in all four ai-signals files. Spot-checked\n88\tcalibration: `open_questions: 1` is consistent with the strategy's \"None\";\n89\t`architecture_claims: 1` rationales cite the actual\n90\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/` files\n91\t(dashboard.md, model-registry.md), which do corroborate the premises used\n92\t(per-run surfaces in the Dashboard, custom properties on ModelVersion as the\n93\tmetadata extension point, Dashboard hosting the registry UI). E004's\n94\t`human_process_gates: -1` is justified by the mandatory technical-review AC\n95\tand publication sign-off. E002's `external_dependency: 0` with a \"neutral\"\n96\trationale was reviewed: the strategy is genuinely silent on whether the