face in the Dashboard via the\n126\tKFP v2 API). Out-of-scope items (auto best-run selection, cross-cluster and\n127\tcross-project comparison) are respected by every epic. Strategy-level\n128\tcontext is carried forward: the spreadsheet-workflow problem statement shapes\n129\tE001's description, the two-council consolidation note shapes the HLR-3\n130\tbundling rationale, and missing strategy sections (teams table, NFRs, formal\n131\tACs) are surfaced as non-blocking Health Warnings rather than silently\n132\tdropped. HLR-4 makes documentation an explicit requirement and E004 fulfills\n133\tit (the strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section, but the\n134\tdocs-authoring epic is present regardless). No conditional branches are\n135\tneeded and none are missing.\n136\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93833fa8a6454cf5","agent_id":"a9ff94ac953f3677e","session_id":"2f8acaed-d2b4-4961-b36e-484262868126","uuid":"e8d3f32b-d850-44e9-9051-376d41056306","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:15:38.009Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fe82e2d8cbabbfa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
